03:49:58,320 --> 03:50:00,980
Yeah, when you drop one earb...

3583
03:50:00,980 --> 03:50:01,940
That happened to me once!

3584
03:50:02,440 --> 03:50:04,680
I was on the way home from the store, and it was at night.

3585
03:50:05,120 --> 03:50:05,840
So it was dark, right?

3586
03:50:06,220 --> 03:50:10,540
And I had a wireless earbud that I paid some money for, it was quite expensive.

3587
03:50:11,020 --> 03:50:14,320
And I was, you know, very happy with it, I was trying to take really good care of it.

3588
03:50:15,020 --> 03:50:19,240
I dropped it, and I stopped walking immediately, because it fell out of my ear, I could notice it immediately.

3589
03:50:19,980 --> 03:50:22,860
I spent half an hour looking for it with my flashlight on my phone.

3590
03:50:23,300 --> 03:50:24,680
I could not find that shit.

3591
03:50:26,340 --> 03:50:30,020
There was no drain, there was no drain, it was just stone, I have no idea, it just disappeared.

3592
03:50:30,680 --> 03:50:31,620
I never saw it again.

3593
03:50:34,080 --> 03:50:34,740
It's crazy.

3594
03:50:39,230 --> 03:50:45,210
I mean, there is a very minute minuscule chance of something facing through, you know, and tunneling.

3595
03:50:45,990 --> 03:50:51,430
It's just very, very unlikely, just like, you know, a glass coming together spontaneously after breaking.

3596
03:50:52,230 --> 03:50:58,490
Theoretically it could happen, but not really theoretically either, because the chances are just so astronomically low.

3597
03:50:59,530 --> 03:50:59,950
It could happen.

3598
03:51:01,570 --> 03:51:02,330
There's a chance.

3599
03:51:04,790 --> 03:51:08,110
New earbuds once have a search function, where you can get them to scream at max volume.

3600
03:51:08,110 --> 03:51:09,270
That's genius.

3601
03:51:12,590 --> 03:51:14,590
I want to customize that.

3602
03:51:15,290 --> 03:51:18,490
You know the meme with the old mummy?

3603
03:51:19,290 --> 03:51:21,030
That they extracted a voice from?

3604
03:51:22,250 --> 03:51:23,110
And he goes...

3605
03:51:24,830 --> 03:51:27,070
I want to customize my own scream.

3606
03:51:29,850 --> 03:51:34,030
When I saw that video for the first time, I laughed for 10 minutes straight.

3607
03:51:34,790 --> 03:51:36,230
It was the funniest shit.

3608
03:51:39,290 --> 03:51:43,990
The people who make that, man, these are the proper comedians of our time.

3609
03:51:46,890 --> 03:51:47,950
Where did you find the notes on the right?

3610
03:51:48,050 --> 03:51:48,590
Just on Google.

3611
03:51:53,480 --> 03:51:59,520
I just Google, like, I don't know, I forgot what I Googled, but Binding of Isaac, Concept Art, or...

3612
03:52:00,800 --> 03:52:04,320
Usually I also write a game name and then press kit or something.

3613
03:52:05,020 --> 03:52:07,420
Usually there's some good stuff in there you can use for inspiration.

3614
03:52:14,160 --> 03:52:18,540
Has Isaac changed your opinion on bullet hells, even if Isaac isn't that hard of a bullet hell?

3615
03:52:19,340 --> 03:52:19,820
It's not?

3616
03:52:21,220 --> 03:52:24,780
Well, then it has not changed my opinion of bullet hells.

3617
03:52:25,240 --> 03:52:29,420
I mean, I am learning to overcome the bullet hell in this game.

3618
03:52:30,540 --> 03:52:33,040
It's not a big deal anymore, as it was in the beginning, for sure.

3619
03:52:34,520 --> 03:52:35,300
Sometimes I get overwhelmed.

3620
03:52:35,500 --> 03:52:39,300
If there's a million enemies and all kinds of shit is happening, my brain just shuts down.

3621
03:52:39,800 --> 03:52:43,380
It happened today, with the Greed run at some point.

3622
03:52:44,000 --> 03:52:45,320
I just can't, you know?

3623
03:52:46,300 --> 03:52:52,140
But when I get into a rhythm and I start to understand, of course it gets easier, and it has gotten easier.

3624
03:52:53,580 --> 03:52:55,840
Your dodging on Hush was on point last stream, thank you.

3625
03:52:56,840 --> 03:52:57,560
I think so too.

3626
03:52:58,440 --> 03:53:00,900
I was in a flow state during that, for sure.

3627
03:53:04,080 --> 03:53:05,020
Exactly, David Dash.

3628
03:53:05,700 --> 03:53:09,340
These are Edmond Macmillan's own notes when he was designing the game, apparently.

3629
03:53:10,800 --> 03:53:17,000
Like the very earliest concept though, you know, scribbling in his notebook about ideas for a game.

3630
03:53:21,390 --> 03:53:21,530
Socks?

3631
03:53:24,630 --> 03:53:25,190
Wait, which socks?

3632
03:53:29,670 --> 03:53:30,990
He admits to smoking flow.

3633
03:53:36,550 --> 03:53:38,370
Yeah, I feel the same way, Flash.

3634
03:53:39,410 --> 03:53:46,010
Like, I can like or learn to love the bullet hell that is Isaac, but I don't think I'm into the genre on its own.

3635
03:53:48,110 --> 03:53:49,310
I think it would be too much.

3636
03:53:49,790 --> 03:53:52,090
Like, I don't enjoy the bullet hell for the bullet hell.

3637
03:53:53,390 --> 03:53:58,850
The thing I love about Isaac so much though is the variety of runs and all the crazy combinations you can get.

3638
03:53:58,950 --> 03:53:59,790
That's the main draw.

3639
03:54:00,730 --> 03:54:03,130
It's not like I go into a boss fight and go, oh shit, nice.

3640
03:54:03,290 --> 03:54:04,810
We got a lot of bullets now.

3641
03:54:05,130 --> 03:54:05,910
This is my jam, you know?

3642
03:54:06,030 --> 03:54:06,990
I like dodging it.

3643
03:54:07,390 --> 03:54:08,510
That's not really the thing.

3644
03:54:09,730 --> 03:54:17,190
Just the sheer variety of builds you can have and crazy stuff happening and the feeling of getting powerful.

3645
03:54:17,990 --> 03:54:21,850
Just that feeling of progression through each run is just so addicting.

3646
03:54:22,490 --> 03:54:23,030
For me.

3647
03:54:26,660 --> 03:54:28,560
Not gonna lie, his handwriting is pretty bad.

3648
03:54:29,860 --> 03:54:31,400
I don't know, I think it's decent.

3649
03:54:32,780 --> 03:54:33,780
I've seen way worse.

3650
03:54:35,040 --> 03:54:37,680
And I was grading high school papers, trust me.

3651
03:54:38,360 --> 03:54:39,840
There's some bad handwriting out there.

3652
03:54:40,840 --> 03:54:42,080
This is not one of them.

3653
03:54:43,860 --> 03:54:46,700
Although I've also heard that doctor's handwriting is pretty bad.

3654
03:54:49,520 --> 03:54:51,580
Alright, it's time for me to eat food.

3655
03:54:52,100 --> 03:54:52,920
Thank you for watching guys.

3656
03:54:53,060 --> 03:54:55,360
This was a fantastic stream.

3657
03:54:56,180 --> 03:54:57,600
So much stuff is happening.

3658
03:54:58,360 --> 03:55:02,800
New areas found, bosses defeated, challenges mastered and conquered.

3659
03:55:03,980 --> 03:55:04,880
Feels good man.

3660
03:55:05,740 --> 03:55:06,760
I'll see you in the next one.

3661
03:55:07,240 --> 03:55:07,440
Bye bye.

3662
03:55:07,900 --> 03:55:08,420
Enjoy your Sunday.
